Date: Fri, 6 Nov 2026 10:56:09 -0500
Subject: fix: a private window follows the settings that hide the address row

The address row's rules are AddressRow, which a normal window's Space model
makes. A private or Guest window has no Space model, so AddressRow::From was
null and BrowserView::IsToolbarVisible never asked: the row stayed with the
address in the sidebar, with the sidebar closed under "Hide the address row
with the sidebar", and against Shift-Cmd-D, and its buttons stayed on it.

The window makes one of its own, beside the page's colour it already makes for
the same reason.

On a Mac the row beside the camera reaches these windows with it. That has not
been tried.

Why: the settings are the person's, in every window (BACKLOG S-439, GitHub
issue 83, private V10).

Removable when: the Space model no longer owns the address row.
